#> tool: awkrepl
#> wait: before Mary:
#> pause: 45
#> must: before Mary: Mark    5.00  20
#> must: last two: Kathy   4.00  10
#> must: Mark    5.00  20
#> not: before Mary: Mary
#> not: last two: Susie
#> source: "last two: "
# 18. Lines by position: the line before a match, and the last two lines. Pement:
#   awk '/regex/{print x};{x=$0}'              the line before the regex
#   awk '{y=x "\n" $0; x=$0};END{print y}'      the last two lines (tail -2)
# Both keep the previous line in a variable. Order matters: the print-before
# rule must run before x is overwritten.
# Try: the line AFTER a match is  /Mary/{getline; print}
/Mary/ { print "before Mary: " x }
{ y = x "\n" $0; x = $0 }
END { print "last two: " y }

#DATA
Beth    4.00  0
Dan     3.75  0
Kathy   4.00  10

Mark    5.00  20
Mary    5.50  22
Susie   4.25  18
Susie   4.25  18
